  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — Canon\n\n**Current state: 0% coverage, no test infrastructure exists.** No `tests/` directory in `engine/`, no test files anywhere in `web/`, no test runner configured for `web/` (package.json has no `test` script or vitest/jest dependency), and `engine/pyproject.toml` lists `pytest` as a dev dependency but has no `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` or `conftest.py`.\n\nMore importantly: **most of the engine is `NotImplementedError` stubs** — this is Phase 1 of a 6-phase build (per `AGENTS.md`), and only a handful of pure functions have real bodies. I've split the gaps below into **(A) implemented code that's untested right now** — highest priority — and **(B) stubbed code that should get TDD skeletons now** so behavior is pinned down before implementation lands, consistent with the project's \"ground truth first\" philosophy.\n\n---\n\n## A. Implemented but untested — fix first\n\n### 1. `engine/pipeline/schema.py` — the tool contract itself has zero tests\n\n`rule_specificity`, the `SurvivorshipRule` validator, `Match.confidence` bounds, and the `CanonModel` camelCase aliasing are all real logic with no coverage. The aliasing behavior in particular is the literal mechanism that keeps `web/` and `engine/` in sync — if it silently breaks, the wire format desyncs without either side's typechecker catching it.\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/pipeline/test_schema.py\nimport pytest\nfrom pydantic import ValidationError\n\nfrom pipeline.schema import CanonModel, Conflict, Match, MatchSignals, SurvivorshipRule, rule_specificity\n\n\nclass TestRuleSpecificity:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n        \"field,entity_type,expected\",\n        [\n            (\"*\", \"*\", 0),\n            (\"*\", \"account\", 1),\n            (\"territory\", \"*\", 2),\n            (\"territory\", \"account\", 3),\n        ],\n    )\n    def test_specificity_score(self, field, entity_type, expected):\n        rule = SurvivorshipRule(\n            id=\"r1\", field=field, entity_type=entity_type,\n            strategy=\"most_recent\", description=\"x\",\n        )\n        assert rule_specificity(rule) == expected\n\n\nclass TestSurvivorshipRuleValidation:\n    def test_prefer_source_without_preferred_source_id_raises(self):\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError, match=\"preferred_source_id\"):\n            SurvivorshipRule(\n                id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\",\n                strategy=\"prefer_source\", description=\"x\",\n            )\n\n    def test_prefer_source_with_preferred_source_id_passes(self):\n        rule = SurvivorshipRule(\n            id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\", strategy=\"prefer_source\",\n            preferred_source_id=\"src-1\", description=\"x\",\n        )\n        assert rule.preferred_source_id == \"src-1\"\n\n    def test_non_prefer_source_strategy_does_not_require_source_id(self):\n        rule = SurvivorshipRule(\n            id=\"r1\", field=\"*\", entity_type=\"*\",\n            strategy=\"escalate\", description=\"x\",\n        )\n        assert rule.preferred_source_id is None\n\n\nclass TestCanonModelAliasing:\n    def test_accepts_camelCase_input(self):\n        m = Match(\n            runId=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\",\n            entityAId=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002\",\n            entityBId=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003\",\n            confidence=0.9, method=\"exact_key\",\n            signals=MatchSignals(exactKey=True, cosine=1.0, fuzzyRatio=100.0),\n        )\n        assert m.entity_a_id is not None\n\n    def test_dump_by_alias_is_camelCase(self):\n        signals = MatchSignals(exact_key=True, cosine=1.0, fuzzy_ratio=100.0)\n        dumped = signals.model_dump(by_alias=True)\n        assert \"exactKey\" in dumped and \"fuzzyRatio\" in dumped\n\n    def test_unknown_field_is_rejected(self):\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\n            MatchSignals(exactKey=True, cosine=1.0, fuzzyRatio=1.0, bogusField=\"x\")\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"confidence\", [-0.01, 1.01])\n    def test_match_confidence_out_of_bounds_rejected(self, confidence):\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\n            Match(\n                runId=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\",\n                entityAId=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002\",\n                entityBId=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003\",\n                confidence=confidence, method=\"exact_key\",\n                signals=MatchSignals(exactKey=True, cosine=1.0, fuzzyRatio=1.0),\n            )\n\n    def test_conflict_rejects_invalid_severity(self):\n        with pytest.raises(ValidationError):\n            Conflict(\n                runId=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001\",\n                matchId=\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002\",\n                field=\"territory\", valueA=\"a\", valueB=\"b\",\n                conflictClass=\"attribute\", severity=5, detectedBy=\"rule\",\n            )\n```\n\n### 2. `engine/agent/graph.py::should_auto_apply` — the auto-apply gate, implemented, zero tests\n\nThis is the single most consequential function in the system (it's the false-auto-apply-rate lever the whole eval sweep is built around) and it currently has no test at all.\n\n```python\n# engine/tests/agent/test_graph.py\nimport pytest\nfrom agent.graph import AUTO_APPLY_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD, AUTO_APPLY_MAX_SEVERITY, should_auto_apply\n\n\nclass TestShouldAutoApply:\n    def test_meets_both_thresholds(self):\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=0.85, severity=2) is True\n\n    def test_confidence_just_below_threshold_rejected(self):\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=0.849, severity=1) is False\n\n    def test_high_confidence_but_severity_too_high_rejected(self):\n        # This is the case that matters most: a model can be very confident\n        # about a structural change and it must STILL escalate.\n        assert should_auto_apply(confidence=0.99, severity=