        "content": "import pytest\nfrom eval.generate import generate\n\npytestmark = pytest.mark.xfail(raises=NotImplementedError, reason=\"Phase 1, not yet implemented\")\n\ndef test_same_seed_produces_identical_manifest(tmp_path):\n    m1 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"a\")\n    m2 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"b\")\n    assert m1 == m2\n\ndef test_different_seeds_produce_different_manifests(tmp_path):\n    m1 = generate(seed=1, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"a\")\n    m2 = generate(seed=2, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"b\")\n    assert m1 != m2\n\ndef test_hierarchy_has_no_cycles(tmp_path):\n    # A synthetic parent/child tree with an accidental cycle would corrupt\n    # every downstream detector — worth a direct check.\n    ...\n\ndef test_every_conflict_class_appears_at_default_rates(tmp_path):\n    manifest = generate(seed=42, accounts=500, out_dir=tmp_path)\n    classes = {m.conflict_class for m in manifest}\n    assert classes == {\"structural\", \"attribute\", \"cosmetic\", \"orphan\", \"duplicate\"}\n\ndef test_ambiguous_entries_expect_escalate(tmp_path):\n    manifest = generate(seed=42, accounts=500, out_dir=tmp_path)\n    ambiguous = [m for m in manifest if m.expected_resolution == \"escalate\"]\n    assert len(ambiguous) > 0\n```\n\n",
