      {
        "title": "C. Integration test gaps",
        "content": "\n| Gap | Why it matters | What to test |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`web/app/api/` is empty** | `AGENTS.md` requires Zod validation on every route handler, but zero route handlers exist yet — this is the largest single gap in the repo, not a missing test | Once `POST /api/runs` exists: creates a `runs` row with status `\"queued\"`, POSTs `{runId}` to the engine, returns immediately without blocking on engine response |\n| **Tool contract drift (Python ↔ Zod)** | Nothing currently enforces that `CanonicalEntity` (Pydantic) and `canonicalEntitySchema` (Zod) accept/reject the same shapes | A shared JSON fixture directory, validated by both `pytest` and `vitest`, so a one-sided edit fails CI instead of surviving to review |\n| **Full pipeline, seed-to-status** | No test exercises extract → normalize → match → detect → resolve → Postgres write → status poll end to end | One `@pytest.mark.integration` test once Phase 1–3 land: `SyntheticConnector` → `execute_run` → assert `runs.status == \"complete\"` with plausible `RunStats` |\n| **Harness against a hand-built micro-manifest** | The full `generate()` output is itself unverified in Phase 1 — testing `harness.py` against it conflates two unverified things | A tiny (5–10 entry) hand-authored manifest with known TP/FP/FN so precision/recall math is checked independently of the generator |\n| **Auto-apply threshold sweep monotonicity** | `sweep_auto_apply_threshold` is the paper's headline figure | Property test: as threshold rises 0.50→0.95, `escalation_rate` is non-decreasing |\n| **`ablate_without_validate`** | The empirical case for `validate` being non-optional | Assert invented-value rate is strictly higher with the node removed than with it present, on the same manifest |\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "D. Missing error-handling coverage (cross-cutting)",
        "content": "\n- **Nothing tests failure paths anywhere yet** — `execute_run` should leave `runs.status = \"failed\"` with a populated `error` field if any stage throws, per its own docstring (\"*a run that fails halfway leaves a readable trail*\"). No test pins this.\n- **`GET /runs/{run_id}/status`** has no \"run not found\" path defined — worth deciding (404 vs. something else) before it's implemented, not after.\n- **Connectors** (`SalesforceConnector`, `WarehouseConnector`) have no documented exception contract for `extract()` — network failure, auth failure, malformed API response are all unhandled today. Worth specifying before Phase 5, since retry/backoff behavior is much cheaper to design in than bolt on.\n- **Model-call failures** in the `propose` node (`agent/graph.py`) — no defined behavior if the Anthropic API errors or times out mid-run. Given rule #3 in `AGENTS.md` (\"escalation is a success state\"), the natural answer is *escalate on API failure rather than crash the run*, but that's not written down anywhere yet — flagging as a design gap, not just a test gap.\n- **Zod `.refine()` on `survivorshipRuleSchema`** — the error path (`[\"preferredSourceId\"]`) is asserted nowhere; if a route handler surfaces raw Zod errors to the UI, an untested error path can silently regress into an unreadable message.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Recommended order of attack",
        "content": "1. **Section A** (6 items above) — real code, zero risk, unblocks CI today with `pytest` (already a dependency) plus approval to add Vitest for `web/`.\n2. **`validate`** and **`should_auto_apply`** tests (already covers the gate; write `validate`'s spec now even before implementing it — it's the one function `AGENTS.md` calls \"non-negotiable\").\n3. Build out `normalize.py`/`detect.py` skeletons alongside their implementation (Phase 2 is next per the build order) — TDD, not after-the-fact.\n4. Table-ownership tests in `db.py` — cheap to write, protects the architectural invariant that's most likely to be violated under time pressure later.\n\nWant me to scaffold the actual `engine/tests/` directory + `conftest.py` fixtures, or set up Vitest for `web/` (needs your go-ahead per the no-new-deps-without-approval rule)?",
        "level": 2
      }
    ],
